# "Instant and sorcery spells you control can't be countered": Bot1's Sphinx of the Final Word is cast in turn 1 (an Island, Black Lotus for
# three and Mox Ruby, Mox Jet and Mox Pearl pay {5}{U}{U}). In turn 3 Bot1 casts Lightning Bolt at Bot2, which answers with Counterspell:
# it may target the Bolt but the Bolt can't be countered, so Bot2 takes 3 (20 -> 17). The control, a creature spell countered with the Sphinx
# in play, is the other scenario; the Sphinx also protects a sorcery, in the third.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Black Lotus
Mox Pearl
Island
Sphinx of the Final Word
Lightning Bolt
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Mox Sapphire
Counterspell
Island x20

